+# 8. Relationship with Other Components
+
+All six original subjects remain with typed component/area and record/contract roles. Actual required edges use consumer→provider under ARC-004/005 with explicit scope, source editions and interfaces. Documentary reference, semantic association, projection, navigation and execution are distinct; no mandatory universal route orcomplete graph is implied.
+
+| Original subject | Kind | Extension responsibility / boundary |
+|---|---|---|
+| Metadata | Component | Descriptor/model/schema/profile/instance owner; Metadata→Document Identity for identity of the applicable normalized document described; actual reciprocal claim below remains |
+| Classification | Component | Category/assignment owner; applicable classified-document key consumption does not allocate DF IDs to every category/entity |
+| Registry | Component | Registration/index owner; intended qualified document/edition/source/freshness evidence; registration is not allocation or a universal intermediary |
+| Relationships | Component | Typed connection/endpoint/provenance owner; document endpoints use identity contracts, other endpoints retain theirs; no silent key creation/retargeting |
+| Knowledge Graph | Component | Logical node/edge projection/properties with authoritative identity/connection source editions/context and refresh limits; no competing semantic ownership |
+| Governance | Area | Workflow, Policies, Reviews, Baselines documentary contracts; actual DMS/tool/manual operation and CMS change scope separate |
+
+The functional DID README states: “The Document Identity component depends on the Metadata component for the canonical definition of metadata concepts used to describe document identity.” Current DID-009§5.1.1/§10 retains Document Identity→Metadata alongside Metadata→Document Identity. Preserve both actual required claims pending responsible core-versus-descriptor/interface/source-edition reconciliation. Different scope names, projection ornavigation relabelling do not dissolve a genuine required cycle; no complete globally acyclic graph is certified.
+
+Governance decisions need actual authority/rules, exact subject/edition/context, executor and observations. Baselines requires exact eligible approved-edition selection and relevant pinned relationship context ortraceable verification evidence. Logical identity orlocal PASS does not approve/publish a Draft successor, select its membership orretarget immutable historical snapshots. Mandatory field/state/lifecycle authority remains pending owner work; no requirement is waived by an extension table.
+
